{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.FullRank","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.FullRank","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.InstanceH2","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Free","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FreeModule.Finite.Basic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.instIsHeckeOfFullRankOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.instIsHeckeOfFullRankOne","kind":"instance","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L225-L227","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.instIsHeckeOfFullRankBase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.instIsHeckeOfFullRankBase","kind":"instance","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L219-L223","doc":"**Base of the induction**: `R` itself is the level-`0` (equivalently\nlevel-`1`) algebra, free of rank `1 = 0! = 1!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.isHeckeOfFullRank_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.isHeckeOfFullRank_succ","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L206-L217","doc":"The two halves composed, as a tower would use them: full rank at level `n`\nplus a rung to `n+1` gives full rank at `n+1`. Stated as its own lemma so a\nconcrete tower can `exact` it inside an `induction`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.finrank_of_rank_recursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.finrank_of_rank_recursion","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L194-L204","doc":"**The numeric induction.** A rank function that starts at `1` and multiplies\nby `n+1` at each rung *is* the factorial. This is the whole content of\n\"assemble inductively\": a tower need only exhibit each rung.\n\nCompare `QOU.Mathlib.HeckeAlgebra.basis_dimension_recurses`, which states the\nsame recursion for `Hn_basis_dimension`; this closes it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.finrank_succ_of_rung","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.finrank_succ_of_rung","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L179-L192","doc":"**One rung of the tower multiplies the rank.** If `A` is free of rank `n+1`\nover `B` and `B` is free of rank `n!` over `R`, then `A` is free of rank\n`(n+1)!` over `R`.\n\nThis is the Iwahori coset decomposition\n`H_{n+1} = ⊕_{i=0}^{n} H_n · (σ_n ⋯ σ_{n-i+1})` in rank form: `n+1` summands,\neach a free rank-one `H_n`-module. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.instIsHeckeOfFullRankH2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.instIsHeckeOfFullRankH2","kind":"instance","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L156-L166","doc":"**`H₂(q)` has the full Hecke rank**, `2 = 2!`. Together with\n`InstanceH2.instHeckeAlgebraH2` this is the first object to satisfy the\n`HeckeAlgebra` class *and* have its dimension pinned.\n\n(The tree's `QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3AlgebraInstance.H3A` and `…HeckeH4AlgebraLaws.H4A`\nare honest Hecke algebras too, with sorry-free Wedderburn isomorphisms giving\ntheir dimensions — they simply had no `HeckeAlgebra` class instance. Wiring this\npredicate to them is the better route; bean qou-awp7.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.finrank_H2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.finrank_H2","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L150-L154","doc":"**`H₂(q)` is free of rank `2` over `R`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.heckePoly_natDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.heckePoly_natDegree","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L145-L148","doc":"…of degree exactly `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.heckePoly_monic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.heckePoly_monic","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L140-L143","doc":"`X² − h·X − 1` is monic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.not_isHeckeOfFullRank_rankOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.not_isHeckeOfFullRank_rankOne","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L117-L126","doc":"More sharply: the rank-one model fails at **every** `n ≥ 2`, since `n! ≥ 2`\nthere. Only `n = 0, 1` — where `H_n(q)` really is one-dimensional — survive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.not_isHeckeOfFullRank_rankOne_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.not_isHeckeOfFullRank_rankOne_three","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L109-L115","doc":"**`ℚ` is not a full-rank Hecke algebra at `n = 3`.** It *is* a\n`HeckeAlgebra ℚ 3 1 ℚ` (`InstanceH2.rankOneModel`), which is exactly why the\nextra predicate is needed: `finrank ℚ ℚ = 1` but `3! = 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsHeckeOfFullRank.finrank_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsHeckeOfFullRank.finrank_eq","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L100-L100","doc":"…of rank exactly `n!` — the Iwahori basis size. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsHeckeOfFullRank.free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsHeckeOfFullRank.free","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L98-L98","doc":"`A` is free as an `R`-module. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsHeckeOfFullRank.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsHeckeOfFullRank.mk","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsHeckeOfFullRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsHeckeOfFullRank","kind":"class","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/FullRank.lean#L82-L100","doc":"**`A` has the full Hecke rank at level `n`**: free over `R` of dimension `n!`.\n\nPair it with `HeckeAlgebra R n q A` at any site that needs `A` to genuinely be\nthe Hecke algebra rather than some quotient satisfying the same relations:\n\n```\nvariable [HeckeAlgebra R n q A] [IsHeckeOfFullRank R n A]\n```\n\nIt is stated without reference to `q` because the dimension of `H_n(q)` does not\ndepend on the parameter.\n","signatureChunk":0}]}